{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"brigandish-weepy-amurminnow","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Summary\n\nFound by the parity census while fixing bug `antelopine-limivorous-chinchilla` (library/MCP reads\nmasking an absent store as an empty one). That fix guards the library read boundary at\n`_reads._tracker()`, which covers the CLI, library, and MCP surfaces. Two AUTOMATED callers\nbypass that boundary entirely by calling the low-level reducer directly, so they retain the old\nsilent behavior on an absent store:\n\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/impossible_links.py:182` — `for state in reduce_all_tickets(tracker_dir)`\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/relation_snapshot.py:257` — `reduced = reduce_all_tickets(...)`\n\nBoth reach `src/rebar/reducer/_api.py:257-260`, which wraps `os.listdir(tracker_path)` in\n`except OSError: return results`. `FileNotFoundError` is an `OSError`, so a missing tracker\nreduces to `[]` with no error.\n\nThe public `rebar.reduce_all_tickets` export (`src/rebar/__init__.py:143,235`) has the same\nproperty. That low-level tolerance is DELIBERATE and was left in place by the sibling fix —\nother callers rely on it — so the correct remedy here is at the two call sites, not in the\nreducer.\n\n## Why this was filed rather than fixed in scope\n\nBoth callers run against a store that has already been established by the time they execute (the\nreconciler after store setup, plan review against a materialized snapshot), so neither is a\nreachable production failure today the way the MCP read surface was. That makes this a latent\nparity gap rather than an active defect, and folding it into the sibling bug would have widened a\nproven single-site fix into a speculative one. Filed so the gap is recorded rather than silently\nleft, per the debug protocol's rule that every MISSING census slot gets an explicit disposition.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `impossible_links` and `relation_snapshot` either resolve their tracker through a guarded\n      boundary, or document why an absent store is legitimately a no-op for them.\n- [ ] Whichever way it is resolved, a test pins the chosen behavior for both call sites against a\n      non-existent tracker directory.\n- [ ] `reducer/_api.py` keeps its `except OSError` tolerance (other callers depend on it) — the\n      fix belongs at the call sites.","id":"cecb-5a41-b8ca-4957","parent_id":"","priority":3,"tags":["store","reads","parity"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Reconciler and plan-review read the reducer directly, bypassing the library read guard on an absent store"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787708686067963001,"uuid":"4482c931-aa39-4d1d-b2ce-750f9705cce4"}